          "text": "Current left eye symptoms and pertinent negatives"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Improving; mild intermittent scratchy sensation and awareness of the left eye, especially at the end of the work day. No significant pain, photophobia, or purulent discharge. Vision reported back to normal. No flashes, floaters, curtain, significant blur, fever, or systemic symptoms."
      }
    },
