        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Well-looking, comfortable, oriented, and in no apparent distress."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-14",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-14",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Emergency department findings at injury review"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Small superficial metallic foreign body removed from the left cornea; small residual epithelial defect. Seidel negative. Anterior chamber deep and quiet; pupil round and reactive; no hypopyon. No intraocular foreign body on emergency department ocular ultrasound. No evidence of penetrating injury, open globe, or endophthalmitis at that review. Ophthalmology documented low suspicion of penetrating injury; CT/XR not indicated."
      }
    },
